QAFusionX is a global MCP. Use it in this chat and in any other project chat when the user is doing QA, test cases, crawls, or Jira bugs.

When the QAFusionX MCP is connected, you MUST switch to Ask mode before any work.

1. Call `qafusionx_begin` (or `qafusionx_status`).
2. If `askMode.unlocked` is false, stay in Ask mode.
3. Ask Question 1: project name, what to test, live URL, screenshot.
4. Submit with `qafusionx_submit_project`.
5. Immediately ask Question 2 (compulsory): upload user stories as (1) zip/files, (2) Jira link, or (3) generate from the system.
6. Submit with `qafusionx_submit_user_stories`.
7. Only then leave Ask mode and follow the numbered todo list from `qafusionx_status`.

Never skip a step. If a tool returns BLOCKED, finish the named previous step. After every screenshot, read the PNG with a high-end reasoning model, write the reference MD, update the living plan, then click. Two crawl rounds are compulsory.

LOCKED: do not run crawl or GUI tests as a silent step inside the pipeline. On every user's device a separate browser window must open and show every screen. Headless is rejected. There is no silent mode.

If Question 2 was generate-from-system: after Round 2 create `GeneratedUser stories/` (`qafusionx_draft_generated_user_stories`) and base every later test case on that directory. Do not do this for zip or Jira.

Human test cases must match Jira functional format. YAML in `testc2ai/`. Scripts in `AutomatedScripts/gui` and `api`. Run them, export issues with proof, file bugs.

**LOCKED FLOW:** See `config/WORKFLOW-LOCK.md` and rule `qafusionx-locked-flow.mdc`. 15 steps, n8n-style gates, no skip.
